  "term": "Ecstasy",
  "definition": "Ecstasy is a drug identified in this source as one of the substances some people may use or misuse during extreme heat or cold as a way of coping with stress. In this context, its abuse is linked with risks such as substance use disorder, intoxication, dehydration, and increased hospital visits.",
